# Pulled & derived data — ignored, with ONE exception.
#
# Negation must be done level by level: un-ignoring a directory wholesale
# (`!data/`) re-includes everything beneath it, which is how 26 MB of prices,
# every derived output, and the old broken anchored Trends pull all got
# committed by accident.
data/*
!data/raw/
data/raw/*

# EXCEPTION: the single-request Trends pull (~350 KB). It cost hours of
# rate-limited pulling — Google caps ~19 requests per ~2.5h window per IP —
# so it is not casually reproducible. Prices (26 MB) are NOT committed: they
# re-pull from yfinance in ~2 minutes, unthrottled.
!data/raw/trends_single/

